b.com/albertcbrown/ard/blob/17c1b80b75973130f6bb18c2f02329a488b5588e/.ard/348/triage-engineer.md) · log [.ard/348/logs/triage-engineer-20261126T080145.999Z.log](https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/blob/17c1b80b75973130f6bb18c2f02329a488b5588e/.ard/348/logs/triage-engineer-20261126T080145.999Z.log) · job `01M8BDZWJY37F689BNK296KQKA` · attempt 1\n\n\n### ard-bot-albertcbrown[bot] at 2026-11-26T08:03:14Z\n\n<!-- ard:triage gate=approval job=01M8BDYJ3JA2T93Y9R8KKHMRS3 -->\n**ard · triage · ready for approval**\n\nTriage is complete; the plan is in `.ard/348/plan.md`. A maintainer adds `ard:approved` to start the `engineer` worker. An approval given before triage finished does not count: remove and re-add the label.\n\n# Plan for #348\n\n## Implementation\n\n### Steps\n\n1. **New `internal/effects` method `SetRepoVariable`.** In `internal/effects/effects.go` add to `Effects`: `SetRepoVariable(ctx context.Context, repo, name, value string) error` (new). Put it beside `ApproveIssue`, not in `github.Writer`, so the App client can never reach it (the App cannot write variables). Implement in a new `internal/effects/variable.go`: `(*Live).SetRepoVariable` validates `repo` with `repopath.Parts`, and a `name` matching `^[A-Z][A-Z0-9_]*$`, then creates or updates the Actions variable (PATCH `repos/{o}/{r}/actions/variables/{name}`, falling back to POST on 404) using the operator token, through go-github (`Actions.CreateRepoVariable` / `UpdateRepoVariable`) on a client built from the token. `(*DryRun).SetRepoVariable` calls `d.emit(ctx, \"SetRepoVariable\", repo, map[string]any{\"name\": name, \"value\": value}, false, nil)` and does nothing else. Log through `l.done`, never the token. Update every other `Effects` implementation or fake (`grep -rn \"ApproveIssue\" internal` shows them; also `internal/effects/archtest` if it lists methods) so the build passes.\n2. **Operator token plumbing.** Add `OperatorToken func(ctx context.Context) (string, error)` to `effects.Options` (`internal/effects/open.go`) and a matching field on `Live` (set via a new option or setter next to `NewLive`). `Live.SetRepoVariable` calls it only when invoked, so the token is read once, held in memory, never logged or stored. When it is nil or fails, return a new exported `effects.ErrNoOperatorToken` with a message naming `ARD_GITHUB_TOKEN` (PAT) and `gh auth login`. In `internal/setupcmd/cmd.go` `Command`, build the func from the existing `github.GhFallback` (`internal/github/ghcli.go`, uses `gh auth token --hostname github.com`) or a PAT `TokenAuth` from `github.AuthFromEnv` when the configured auth is a PAT. Reuse what #302 already put in `internal/github/auth.go`; do not add a second token reader. If the configured auth is the App, use the gh fallback.\n3. **Embedded workflow.** New directory `internal/setupcmd/workflow/` (new) with `bot-commits.yml`, a byte-for-byte copy of `.github/workflows/bot-commits.yml` (copying into a new path is allowed; do not edit `.github/`). New `internal/setupcmd/workflow.go`: `//go:embed workflow/bot-commits.yml` into `var botCommitsWorkflow []byte`, `const workflowPath = \".github/workflows/bot-commits.yml\"`, and `PrintWorkflow(w io.Writer) error` writing the bytes.\n4. **Workflow check row.** In `workflow.go` add `func checkWorkflow(ctx, fileAt func(ctx, rev, path string) ([]byte, bool, error)) Row` (name `workflow`). Absent on `origin/main` gives `StatusManual` with detail `commit .github/workflows/bot-commits.yml: run ard setup --print-workflow > .github/workflows/bot-commits.yml, then open a PR`. Different bytes (compare after normalising CRLF to LF) gives `StatusManual`, with the same fix and \"differs from the copy embedded in ard\". Equal gives `StatusOK`. If `origin/main` does not exist, give a `StatusManual` row saying it could not be checked (fetch first), never a hard failure. Add `Deps.WorkflowAt func(ctx context.Context) ([]byte, bool, error)` (new) in `internal/setupcmd/setup.go`; wire it in `cmd.go` with `gitx.New(\"\").FileAt(ctx, root, \"origin/main\", workflowPath, 1<<20)` (`internal/gitx/local.go`). Append the row in `Run` after the policy rows, before the label step, only when `WorkflowAt != nil`. Setup never commits and never writes `.github/`.\n5. **ARD_BOT_LOGIN row and apply.** In `internal/setupcmd/setup.go` add `Deps.Variables VariableWriter` (new interface `SetRepoVariable(ctx, repo, name, value string) error`) and `Deps.Confirm func(prompt string) (bool, error)` (new). Add `botLoginVar = \"ARD_BOT_LOGIN\"` in `policy.go`. New `botLoginRow` in `workflow.go` or a new `botlogin.go`: want is `id.Login`, taken from `Policy.Identity` (already used in `policyRows`; make sure it ends in `[bot]`, otherwise a `StatusManual` row \"ard is not running as a GitHub App; ARD_BOT_LOGIN needs the App's <slug>[bot] login\"). Never read config for it. Read the current value with `Policy.GetVariable`. Absent gives `StatusDrift` (\"not set; will set to <want>\"). Equal gives ok. Different gives `StatusDrift` (\"is <have>, App is <want>\"). Soft errors (`ErrForbidden`, `ErrNotFound`) give a manual row with `gh variable set ARD_BOT_LOGIN -R <repo> --body <want>`. Apply, in `Run`, after the checks, only when not `Check`, not blocked, and the row is drift: absent, call `SetRepoVariable`; different, call `Confirm` first and skip with a `StatusManual` row (fix command in detail) when it answers no or is nil. Under dry-run the writer logs only and the row says \"would set\". `ErrNoOperatorToken` or a write error becomes a manual row with the `gh variable set` command, not an abort. Set the variable before the labels so a label failure does not hide it.\n6. **Confirmation prompt.** In `cmd.go` build `Confirm` from `e.Stdin` if `cli.Env` has it (check `internal/cli/app.go`; if it has no stdin or the input is not a terminal, return false so the run never blocks or overwrites silently). Add `--yes` only if the existing `cli.Env` has no prompt helper to reuse; otherwise keep to the flags in step 7